; Golden expansion tests for the mutation instrumenter: one fixture per
; operator (neg, cmp, con, ari), one per placement rule that bites
; (nesting, chain), one per exclusion (shadowed operators, assert, lazy,
; inline tests in both spellings, excluded file, a file with nothing to
; mutate), one per [[@mutate off]] spelling, and two for the silent edges
; of the dismissal grammar (off_edges, off_unclosed) - the positions
; where a well-formed attribute is ignored without a diagnostic, which
; are exactly the ones a reader cannot discover from the code.
; pp.exe is a standalone ppxlib
; driver linking the rewriter; each fixture .ml is expanded
; (with-stdout-to) or rejected (with-accepted-exit-codes 1, capturing the
; diagnostic) and diffed against a committed .expected golden.
;
; The goldens pin the exact generated bytes: site indexes, byte extents,
; line and column numbers, the rendered before/after text, and the shape
; of every guard. That is their job - editing a fixture reshuffles them,
; so read every promoted diff. Accept intended changes with dune promote.
; The fixtures are not compiled: only pp is a module, and
; integration/ compiles the generated code for real.

(executable
 (name pp)
 (modules pp)
 (libraries ppxlib windtrap_mutate_ppx))

; Expansion goldens

(rule
 (with-stdout-to
  fixture_neg.actual
  (run ./pp.exe --impl %{dep:fixture_neg.ml})))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff fixture_neg.expected fixture_neg.actual)))

